35
00:04:41.864 --> 00:04:48.356
into the darkness. Raoul let out a sigh of relief, and the Persian laughed. "I should have remembered the

36
00:04:49.242 --> 00:04:56.652
opera house has a ratcatcher," the Persian said. "His lantern was focused on his face, so he wouldn't scare

37
00:04:56.852 --> 00:05:02.389
the rats. That's why he looked so strange." The Persian wanted to rest for a moment, but Raoul

38
00:05:02.390 --> 00:05:09.277
was full of questions and plans. "Are we very far from the lake now? When will we get there?

39
00:05:09.278 --> 00:05:15.266
When we arrive, we'll call out, and Christine will hear us. Of course, he'll hear us too, but he

40
00:05:15.267 --> 00:05:25.292
knows you, so we'll—" "Hush!" the Persian interrupted. "We'll never enter his house from the lake because it's too

