43
00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:50.156
the siren singing. I've never been inside his house—" "What?" Raoul exploded with anger and impatience. "Then how can

44
00:05:50.157 --> 00:05:57.082
you help Christine?" The Persian tried to calm the young man. "Our only hope is to enter the

45
00:05:57.083 --> 00:06:05.372
house unnoticed by him." "But how do we enter the house without crossing the lake?" "I know the exact

46
00:06:05.373 --> 00:06:12.714
spot—even though I've never used it myself. It's where the old scenery is stored, the place where Joseph Buquet's

47
00:06:12.715 --> 00:06:18.117
body was found. We must return to the third cellar and hope that everyone has left by now so

48
00:06:18.118 --> 00:06:24.749
we can use the secret entrance." Raoul followed his guide back up to the third cellar, where they squeezed

49
00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:34.551
between two old sets—a farmhouse and a throne room. "Sit down and rest for a few minutes," the Persian

50
00:06:35.675 --> 00:06:43.645
said, taking a seat on the floor and inviting Raoul to sit next to him. "Why?" Raoul remained standing.

51
00:06:44.189 --> 00:06:51.792
"Every minute we waste is another minute Christine is a prisoner." "Before we enter his house—a most dangerous

52
00:06:51.793 --> 00:07:02.643
place—I want to tell you my history with him. That way you'll trust me and do everything I say."

53
00:07:02.697 --> 00:07:05.730
"Aren't you worried he'll overhear us?" The Persian shook his head. "This floor is made of stone, as are

54
00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:20.594
the walls of his house, which means once we enter, no one outside the house will hear our screams."

